      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "From the results of intraoperative examination of 50 patients with ischemic heart disease it is shown that the collateral blood flow has an essential effect on the detection of the signs of myocardial ischemia. Aortocoronary shunting leads to positive dynamics of regional myocardial function. The test with compression of the shunt may be used for indirect appraisal of the efficacy of myocardial revascularization."},
